   <refbody>  
     <section>
    <p>Consider a concept section titled "Connection Modes" where the author has used a native HTML <codeph>&lt;dl&gt;</codeph> element with <codeph>&lt;dt&gt;</codeph> and <codeph>&lt;dd&gt;</codeph> pairs.</p>
       <table frame="all" colsep="1" rowsep="1">
         <title>Native dl/dt/dd list element</title>
         <tgroup cols="2">
           <colspec colname="c1"/>
           <colspec colname="c2"/>
           <thead>
             <row>
               <entry>
                 <b>HTML Input</b>
               </entry>
               <entry>
                 <b>DITA Output</b>
               </entry>
             </row>
           </thead>
           <tbody>
             <row>
               <entry>
                 <codeblock>
&lt;h2 id="connection-modes">Connection Modes&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>
  The device supports the following connection modes.
&lt;/p>
&lt;dl>
  &lt;dt>Wired&lt;/dt>
  &lt;dd>
    Uses an Ethernet cable to connect the device directly to the network switch.
  &lt;/dd>
  &lt;dt>Wireless&lt;/dt>
  &lt;dd>
    Connects the device using the built-in Wi-Fi adapter.
  &lt;/dd>
  &lt;dt>Bluetooth&lt;/dt>
  &lt;dd>
    Pairs the device with a host computer for short-range data transfer.
  &lt;/dd>
&lt;/dl></codeblock>
               </entry>
               <entry>
                 <codeblock>
&lt;concept id="connection_modes">
  &lt;title>Connection Modes&lt;/title>
  &lt;conbody>
    &lt;p>The device supports the following connection modes.&lt;/p>
    &lt;dl>
      &lt;dlentry>
        &lt;dt>Wired&lt;/dt>
        &lt;dd>
          &lt;p>Uses an Ethernet cable to connect the device directly to the network switch.&lt;/p>
        &lt;/dd>
      &lt;/dlentry>
      &lt;dlentry>
        &lt;dt>Wireless&lt;/dt>
        &lt;dd>
          &lt;p>Connects the device using the built-in Wi-Fi adapter.&lt;/p>
        &lt;/dd>
      &lt;/dlentry>
      &lt;dlentry>
        &lt;dt>Bluetooth&lt;/dt>
        &lt;dd>
          &lt;p>Pairs the device with a host computer for short-range data transfer.&lt;/p>
        &lt;/dd>
      &lt;/dlentry>
    &lt;/dl>
  &lt;/conbody>
&lt;/concept></codeblock>
               </entry>
             </row>
           </tbody>
         </tgroup>
       </table>
      
       <p>
            <b>Result:</b> The native HTML <codeph>&lt;dl&gt;</codeph> structure maps directly to DITA. The mapping is: <codeph>&lt;dl&gt;</codeph> → <codeph>&lt;dl&gt;</codeph>; each <codeph>&lt;dt&gt;</codeph> → <codeph>&lt;dlentry&gt;&lt;dt&gt;</codeph>; each <codeph>&lt;dd&gt;</codeph> → <codeph>&lt;dlentry&gt;&lt;dd&gt;&lt;p&gt;</codeph>.</p>
  </section>
   </refbody>
